---
const features = [
  {
    title: "Steady workspace context",
    body:
      "Authentication, project selection, and workspace state are explicit so users can continue from where they were, even after refresh or restart."
  },
  {
    title: "Human-led content execution",
    body:
      "Each screen keeps review, status, and workflow transitions explicit so teams stay in control instead of surrendering decisions."
  },
  {
    title: "Resilient API behavior",
    body:
      "Degraded mode keeps browsing the app useful when services are unavailable, with clear queues for supported actions."
  },
  {
    title: "Operational visibility",
    body:
      "Uptime, performance, diagnostics, and activity surfaces show what is healthy and what is waiting."
  }
];
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why ContentFlow App Exists</p>
    <h2>Most teams fail at continuity before they fail at ideas.</h2>
    <p>
      ContentFlow App exists to keep operators from losing momentum when tools,
      APIs, or context boundaries shift mid-workflow.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card-grid">
    {
      features.map((feature) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h3>{feature.title}</h3>
          <p>{feature.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>
